# Secrets — never commit. .env holds JWT_SECRET and the LLM API keys.
/.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local database and uploaded files. storage/ is app state, not source:
# committing a .db means every clone shares one database and every conflict
# is an unreviewable binary merge.
storage/*.db
storage/*.db-wal
storage/*.db-shm
storage/*.sqlite
storage/*.sqlite-wal
storage/*.sqlite-shm
# Backups and side-copies of the database are the same category: real user
# rows and password hashes, not source. *.db.bak does not match *.db.
storage/*.bak
storage/*.db.*
storage/*.db2
storage/*.old
storage/uploads/
storage/.smoke_token
storage/cache/
storage/*.log

# Dependencies
/vendor/

# Agent state written during a session. Protected from modification for the
# same reason as .env, and these files are IJFW-owned session state — do not
# read or rewrite them, only keep them out of commits.
.ijfw/.session-signals.jsonl
.ijfw/.session-feedback.jsonl
.ijfw/.prompt-check-state

# IJFW tool state — session logs, metrics, dream-state and its code index.
# Local tooling bookkeeping, not project source: it records how a machine
# happened to work on this repo and changes on every session. The three
# protected files below stay out for the same reason and are IJFW-owned —
# never read or rewrite them.
.ijfw/
ijfw/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
# Windows device-name artifact: a mistyped sqlite invocation writes its
# error text to a file called "nul" (Windows treats NUL as a device, not a name).
# Never source content; it is not a real file.
nul
